The source and ordinary portable distributions use an external Node.js runtime.
The optional Windows desktop bundle includes an official Node.js executable
and its complete upstream LICENSE in runtime/NODE_LICENSE.txt, including
third-party notices. Exact version, source URL and SHA-256 are in manifest.json.
Node built-in modules provide filesystem/process and standard crypto support.
The backup engine's content hashing uses the MoonBit crypto dependency.

The original Windows launcher uses the OS-provided .NET Framework and Windows
Forms. These operating-system components are not redistributed by this project.
